@API = http://localhost:3000/api/v1

### 1  Login as the padel coach (user 2, not in tennis)
POST {{API}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "coach.padel@example.com",
  "password": "abdellahnsila123#002"
}

### 2  Status (expect is_member false, has_pending_request false)
GET {{API}}/clubs/tennis/status

### 3  Ask to join (expect { "status": "pending" })
POST {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join

### 4  Ask again (expect the same answer, still ONE row in the database)
POST {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join

### 5  Status (expect has_pending_request true)
GET {{API}}/clubs/tennis/status

### 6  Cancel (expect { "success": true })
DELETE {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join

### 7  Cancel again (expect 404)
DELETE {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join

### 8  Ask again after cancelling (expect pending, the SAME row is reopened)
POST {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join

### 9  Join your own club (expect 409)
POST {{API}}/clubs/padel/join

### 10  Club that does not exist (expect 404)
POST {{API}}/clubs/not-a-club/join